# {{project.name}}

```
xlings install qemu-arm -y      # once, per machine
mcpp run --target aarch64-none-elf
```

⚠️ **The first line is not optional, and leaving it out fails in a way that
names itself.** `mcpp.toml` declares the emulator through the board package, and
a declaration is not an install trigger. Without it the build SUCCEEDS and says:

```
warning: aarch64-virt-rt: qemu-arm is not installed, so `mcpp run` has no runner.
```

## What the board supplies

The memory map (`virt.ld`), the entry point that parks the secondary cores and
zeroes `.bss`, a PL011 console, and the emulator command line. This project
names none of them — no load address, no UART address, no `-nostdlib`.

## The zero-libc tier

There is no C library. `board::print_uint` exists because a board with no libc
still has to be able to show a number, and it is the smallest thing that is not
a formatter.

A project that wants `printf` declares `xim:picolibc-aarch64` — which is this
project's decision to make, not the board's.
